{
  "reference_answer": "Yes, I do prefer working from home, mainly because it saves me a lot of commuting time. That extra hour or so each day adds up, and I can use it to exercise or just start work earlier when my mind is fresh. I also find I concentrate better at home since there are fewer interruptions than in a busy office. That said, I wouldn't want to do it every single day. I miss the casual chats with colleagues, and sometimes talking things through face to face is much quicker than sending messages back and forth. So on balance, I'd go for a hybrid arrangement, maybe two or three days at home and the rest in the office.",
  "reference_angle_summary": "独立主线：以通勤时间与专注度为主要理由，承认办公室社交与沟通优势，最终倾向混合办公；示例不代表用户经历。",
  "takeaway_expressions": [
    {
      "expression": "adds up",
      "meaning_zh": "积少成多；累计起来很可观",
      "why_useful": "谈论时间、金钱或小习惯的累积影响时非常自然，口语高频。",
      "example": "Saving twenty minutes a day doesn't sound like much, but it adds up over a year.",
      "usage_note": "通常用主动形式，主语多为时间、费用、小变化等。"
    },
    {
      "expression": "on balance",
      "meaning_zh": "权衡之后；总的来说",
      "why_useful": "在比较利弊后给出最终倾向时很实用，比 in conclusion 更口语化。",
      "example": "On balance, I think the benefits of living alone outweigh the drawbacks.",
      "usage_note": "常放在句首，后接最终判断或选择。"
    },
    {
      "expression": "go for a hybrid arrangement",
      "meaning_zh": "选择混合办公安排",
      "why_useful": "讨论工作方式时很具体，也能自然表达折中方案，避免只说 advantages。",
      "example": "I'd go for a hybrid arrangement so I get both flexibility and team contact.",
      "usage_note": "go for 表示选择、倾向；hybrid arrangement 可替换为 flexible setup。"
    }
  ]
}

